{"id": "20876", "revid": "2253620", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=20876", "title": "Maineville (Ohio)", "text": "Maineville is a city in Warren County, Southwest Ohio.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nFrom Interstate I-71, take Ohio Exit 28 south on State Route 48 approximately 3.5 miles to the intersection of State Route 48 with Montgomery Road (State Route 22 &amp; 3), then another 1.6 miles south on State Route 48 to downtown for the City of Maineville as reckoned by the intersection of Foster-Maineville Road and State Route 48.\nOne may also reach downtown Maineville by taking the Montgomery Road exit from I-275, driving north 8.4 miles, then turning south (right) on State Route 48 1.6 miles.\nThe Maineville zip code of 45039 also encompasses Hamilton Township, Warren County and the unincorporated area of Landen.\nBy plane.\nMaineville situated between three major airports:\nEach airport can be accessed from Maineville with at least some portion of interstate driving.\nEstimated driving times from Maineville to the airports are:"}
